From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe-17x: Add parameters and statistics nodes to the pixel path

Expose the Titan 17x IFE pixel pipeline to a userspace 3A through two
video nodes per full VFE:

- msm_vfeN_pix_params (META_OUTPUT) takes V4L2 extensible ISP parameter
  buffers with black level, white balance, colour correction, gamma and
  AWB grid blocks. One buffer is applied at stream start, then one per
  frame from the CAMIF epoch 0 interrupt (line 20), followed by a PIX
  register update. Gamma curves are written to the inactive DMI banks
  before the bank select flips.
- msm_vfeN_pix_stats (META_CAPTURE) buffers are the target of the AWB
  Bayer grid write master (WM 15, PLAIN64, frame based); without a queued
  buffer the master writes a driver scratch buffer.

Number the pixel path images and statistics by the CAMIF epochs since
the stream start, so images, statistics and parameters keep the same
frame numbers when the driver runs out of image buffers or the grid
starts late, and send a V4L2_EVENT_FRAME_SYNC from the pixel subdev at
each epoch for the sensor control timing in userspace.

The register layouts come from the SC8280XP Windows camera stack and were
checked on the hardware: CC12 rows G, B, R; gamma bank select bits G, B,
R; AWB grid records { sum[R, B, Gr, Gb], count[...] } taken after the
black level and before the white balance. The UAPI is in
include/uapi/linux/media/qcom/ife17x-config.h.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
